{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n2le01ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n2le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "text": "<p><strong>Geraldine</strong>: Brandon! How nice to see you again.</p>\n<strong>Brandon</strong>: Hi, Geraldine, long time no see.</p>\n<strong>Geraldine</strong>: Yes, I know, I was a little busy the last term; I had to study hard because there was a topic I found difficult to understand.</p>\n<p><strong>Brandon</strong>: Really? What topic was that?</p>\n<p><strong>Geraldine</strong>: We studied the Kernel language approach.</p>\n<p><strong>Brandon</strong>: Oh! The Kernel language, I had to study that approach some years ago, and you are right, for me, it was also hard to grasp.</p>", "time": "100"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob10re2img02.jpg", "text": "<p><strong>Geraldine</strong>: Yeah, but now I know that the Kernel language translates all language constructs from a core language to ease the understanding of the program functionality. And that it consists of two parts; the first one defines a simple language, which is very easy to implement and also improves efficiency. The second one defines a translation scheme from all the programming languages to the Kernel language. We just need to be careful to differentiate those two aspects of the Kernel language.</p>\n<p><strong>Brandon</strong>: There are also two kinds of translation, I remember I was always afraid to forget their names during the exams. They are the namely linguistic abstraction and the syntactic sugar; the former refers to constructs that we added to the language syntax; this extends the language and contributes to its purposes; the latter provides short-cut notations to reduce the size of the language so to improve its readability.</p>", "time": "31000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob10re2img03.jpg", "text": "<p><strong>Geraldine</strong>: You did learn those concepts by heart. Did you learn about the approaches to the Kernel language?</p>\n<p><strong>Brandon</strong>: Yes, I did. There are four main approaches to the Kernel language semantics: a) an operational semantics approach that shows us how a statement works, b) an axiomatic semantics approach which focuses on the main relations between the inputs, c) a denotational semantics approach shows us the functionality over an abstract domain, and d) the logical semantics approach which defines a statement as a model of a logical theory.</p>\n<p><strong>Geraldine</strong>: I see, You didn't waste your time in class, Brandon, I feel lucky to run into you.</p>", "time": "99000"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can explain briefly what the Kernel language approach is. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify information related to formal logistics.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about the approaches related to language semantics.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you consider language approaches important? why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you know  any language approach?  Which one?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_t